{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/345586-shadowguiding-and-harrowing-in-w20-questions-from-a-potential-player","id":345586,"title":"Shadowguiding and Harrowing in W20: Questions from a potential player","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-20T02:12:14-08:00","id":345586,"title":"Shadowguiding and Harrowing in W20: Questions from a potential player","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> This is my first post here. I used to play lots of RPG when I was younger and Vampire was my favorite. However, I have kept hearing good things about Wraith but never read or tried the game. I now see there is a kickstarter for a new edition of Wraith, which has caught my interest.<br /> <br /> Reading reviews of the old 2e Wraith it seems like the overwhelming majority of them stresses how depressing the game is (and bleak, and dark, etc). I did want to take a look for myself though, and got hold of the pdf for the 2e and have read that from cover to cover. While I can see were the bleaknessand horror comments might come from (the art with the secretary with fleshhooks comes to mind...I like the more suggestive art), I also see a very deep and engaging world full of interesting opertunities for adventure and fun games.<br /> <br /> The two sections, while interesting, were I see my group might run into problems is the shadowguiding and harrowing sections as I get a somehwat antagonistic vibe (I don't want my players to start throwing the cutlery). Will the new rule sinclude options for lessening the more antagonistic/evil aspects of shadow and harrowing while still keeping them as mechanics? I see some allusions to this in the feature list of the kickstarter but more information before pledging would be nice. Will there be a sample chapter released later in the kickstarter for those of us who are on the fence?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4574-laughing-lord","name":"Laughing Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T19:11:09-08:00","id":346317,"title":"","content":"There's the <i>Shadow Player's Guide</i> and <i>The Sea of Shadows</i> books. Both add onto the material on Shadowguiding and Harrowings respectively. Undoubtedly some of that knowledge will find its way into Wr20 and Dansky has mentioned that they'll make it a little more accessible. But until its released or they give us some more previews on the material I can't say.<br /> <br /> I will say this though, WtO may seem like the bleakest, darkest, most depressing game of the OWoD but beneath that outer layer there are themes of spirituality and hope. In fact of all the lines its the only one that has a definable end goal in the Rulebook. No matter how powerful a vampire becomes there's always a bigger vampire out there. No matter how many Wyrm minions and Weaver slaves your werewolf destroys there's always more out there coming from you. But in WtO you've died and become stuck in a bad situation yet despite all that you have a means to escape, by overcoming your characters baggage, their demons, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T22:07:41-08:00","id":346463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Laughing Lord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/345586-shadowguiding-and-harrowing-in-w20-questions-from-a-potential-player#post345586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The two sections, while interesting, were I see my group might run into problems is the shadowguiding and harrowing sections as I get a somehwat antagonistic vibe (I don't want my players to start throwing the cutlery). Will the new rule sinclude options for lessening the more antagonistic/evil aspects of shadow and harrowing while still keeping them as mechanics? I see some allusions to this in the feature list of the kickstarter but more information before pledging would be nice. Will there be a sample chapter released later in the kickstarter for those of us who are on the fence?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to get much broader options for Shadowguiding and Harrowings. Lillian and Mikko are still working on this, so I can't throw specifics at you, but this is one of the first things I mentioned to Rich Thomas when we started discussing what changes Wraith 20 needed to make. <br /> <br /> -deadguy out","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1052-realdeadguy","name":"RealDeadguy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1052_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T03:35:43-08:00","id":346564,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your replies. It makes it clearer.<br /> <br /> What I am looking for in Wraith is a good medium to tell ghost stories of different flavours. That is, I want a game with the tools to play both scary (lthe ring), mysterious (undead x-files) and adventure stories. Looking at the outline of the storyteller chapter in the sample of chapter 1 it seems the game will cater to a broad spectrum of themes. Great!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Just adding this. Idealy the broader options would mean that shadow and harrowing would be there when I want the personal/horror type game, but their impact could be lessened when I want the undead adventure game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4574,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4574-laughing-lord","user":"Laughing Lord","date":". 12-21-2014, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4574-laughing-lord","name":"Laughing Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T21:58:49-08:00","id":347160,"title":"","content":"Since everyone else has chimed in about the posted topic, I just want to add that for my money, Wraith isn't really all that depressing, especially compared most of the other White Wolf games. If you want depressing, then you should look up Vampire, Werewolf, or Changeling.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T12:21:49-07:00","id":446362,"title":"","content":"You could pinch the Kindred of the East style of 'Shadowguiding', if it's too dark for your group. Basically, represent the Shadowguiding with contested rolls between Shadow and Psyche. Likewise, Harrowings could be a series of contested rolls, or just one (but that puts too much emphasis on luck, given the results of a failure or a botch).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}